    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0205" n="939" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg939"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Baron
                            Fava.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-03-13"><hi rendition="#italic">March 13,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 8.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Baron</hi>: Your note of to-day’s date
                    relating to the press reports of the killing of four Italian laborers at
                    Walsenburg, Colo., has been received.</p>
                <p>I have telegraphed the governor of Colorado for information on the subject, and
                    upon receipt of a reply from him will promptly advise you.</p>
                <p>Very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
